    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The investigation of the benthic Foraminifera of the South Shetland Island,\nallowed us to detect the presence of abundant units of E. parva in Caleta\nBalleneros and Puerto Foster stations  (Deception Island), which in addition\nshowed a wide morphologic variation of the shell. Ten summit sediment samples\nwere recovered with the purpose of carrying out a census of the Foraminifera\npopulation. These Foraminifera presented a remarkable variation in the form of\nthe shells, illustrating the reason why they have been determined like\nCassidulinoides parkerianus by some authors. Its distribution is restricted to\nthe south of the Antarctica convergence: Ross and Weddel Seas and Bransfield\nStrait.",
